00:14:21.818 --> 00:14:25.331
If an Amish person
can build your barn, or shed, or house,

00:14:25.398 --> 00:14:28.213
you're a lucky person
'cause that's what you want.

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:29.606
They do quality work.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.050
[man] Come in to the right!

00:14:32.836 --> 00:14:34.162
[Peter] Number seven!

00:14:35.928 --> 00:14:39.078
So Gus's is a local favorite I believe.

00:14:39.145 --> 00:14:42.328
We're not gonna wait in that line
but what we're gonna do now is…

00:14:42.775 --> 00:14:45.220
well, if you've seen my videos before,

00:14:45.647 --> 00:14:48.824
you know we're not gonna
keep in the nice touristy areas

00:14:48.891 --> 00:14:52.025
so we're gonna jump the tracks,
go to another part of Philly,

00:14:52.092 --> 00:14:55.270
and then come back for the action.

00:14:56.104 --> 00:14:57.512
The build up to the game.

00:14:57.969 --> 00:14:59.799
And catch those festivities.

00:14:59.866 --> 00:15:02.340
But before then
we're going on a little mission.

00:15:05.462 --> 00:15:07.027
A little pit stop here, guys.

00:15:07.094 --> 00:15:09.215
At the Simon and Schuster Warehouse.

00:15:09.282 --> 00:15:12.345
We're gonna see my book
for the first time together

00:15:12.412 --> 00:15:14.450
-How you doing?
-Good, how are you doing?

00:15:14.517 --> 00:15:17.050
-Doing well. Exciting day.
-[laughs]

00:15:17.884 --> 00:15:20.052
-When did my book get in?
-Thursday.

00:15:20.119 --> 00:15:22.851
-Waiting out here for you.
-Oh, cool. Wow!

00:15:22.918 --> 00:15:23.801
Look at this.

00:15:24.624 --> 00:15:27.093
-This is the pallets of your book.
-No way.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.595
-These are all my book?
-These are all your book.

00:15:29.662 --> 00:15:31.384
Someone already broke into 'em.

00:15:31.451 --> 00:15:32.334
[laughter]

00:15:33.005 --> 00:15:34.100
Guilty, yeah.

00:15:34.167 --> 00:15:36.589
-Mike, you're going camera man.
-Sure.

00:15:37.003 --> 00:15:38.718
All right, the big moment.

00:15:38.785 --> 00:15:39.668
-Here you go.

00:15:41.779 --> 00:15:42.973
[laughter]

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.813
All right. Here it is.

00:15:45.501 --> 00:15:48.091
Everyone, Your Fellow Americans.

00:15:48.581 --> 00:15:51.082
Okay, all the spelling's right,
we're good on that.

00:15:51.149 --> 00:15:52.819
Doesn't say your fellow Mexicans.

00:15:52.886 --> 00:15:54.566
-It's been proofread. [laughs]

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:57.650
Wow, I love the feel of this too.

00:15:57.717 --> 00:15:58.600
-Yeah.

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:01.122
It's got a glossy feel and then hear that?

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:03.873
[scraping]

00:16:04.882 --> 00:16:05.956
It's got texture.

00:16:08.591 --> 00:16:10.149
-Goosebumps.
-Goosebumps.

00:16:10.216 --> 00:16:12.454
Haven't gotten those in a while.

00:16:12.839 --> 00:16:14.398
So there you go, guys,

00:16:14.465 --> 00:16:16.475
pre-order Your Fellow Americans.

00:16:16.542 --> 00:16:19.041
It goes live on August 4th.

00:16:19.383 --> 00:16:21.404
QR code here, link down below.

00:16:21.471 --> 00:16:23.487
Also the book tour is happening.

00:16:24.057 --> 00:16:29.389
Gonna be in New York, Boston,
Greater Chicago, Greater Detroit,

00:16:29.456 --> 00:16:30.416
Greater Phoenix.

00:16:30.483 --> 00:16:34.051
We just added LA and more dates coming.

00:16:34.476 --> 00:16:36.697
So hope to see you
at one of those signings.

00:16:36.764 --> 00:16:39.593
We'll all hang out.
It'll be great to see you in person.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.012
Thanks, you guys.

00:16:41.079 --> 00:16:42.318
This is a special day.

00:16:42.385 --> 00:16:45.449
Without these guys, none of this happens.
Hey, don't walk out.

00:16:45.516 --> 00:16:47.089
-You're back in there.
-[laughter]

00:16:47.156 --> 00:16:49.306
Without these guys, none of this happens.

00:16:49.373 --> 00:16:52.162
This is behind the scenes
of how the book world works.

00:16:52.586 --> 00:16:54.428
Not only is it the editors,

00:16:54.795 --> 00:16:59.197
and the book cover designers,
it's the people that actually facilitate

00:16:59.264 --> 00:17:01.748
you getting the book.

00:17:01.815 --> 00:17:05.389
Huge operation with a lot of logistics.

00:17:05.456 --> 00:17:07.246
and hard-working passionate people

00:17:07.977 --> 00:17:09.833
-So thank you guys.
-Thank you.

00:17:18.835 --> 00:17:22.497
[Peter] Malcom, born and raised in Philly.
How's it going right now?

00:17:22.564 --> 00:17:24.153
Just doing a little Uber today.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:27.013
It's the World Cup going on,
a lot going on in the city.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.112
So what have you been doing, Malcom?
You've got your own what?

00:17:30.179 --> 00:17:32.725
Luxury designer brand
called Savage Series 8.

00:17:32.799 --> 00:17:34.924
Got New York Fashion Week
coming up in September.

00:17:34.991 --> 00:17:36.553
-Nice, you wearing these clothes?

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.550
This is one of my sweatsuits,
it's one of one, custom made.

00:17:39.617 --> 00:17:40.719
Nobody else got this.

00:17:40.786 --> 00:17:44.346
Do you think I could get away with
wearing that? Could I pull that off?

00:17:44.413 --> 00:17:46.448
Yeah, you got style.

00:17:46.515 --> 00:17:49.773
You're being nice, Malcom.
I got a black shirt and dorky shoes.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.133
-But you love your city?
-Of course, for sure.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.887
I was born in the inner city.

00:17:53.954 --> 00:17:56.785
So that's even more of a way
to see how Philly have grown

00:17:56.852 --> 00:17:58.269
in so many years.

00:17:58.897 --> 00:18:02.863
It's unbelievable to even see it
'cause it's such a hustle mentality city.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.032
The grit, the culture.

00:18:06.248 --> 00:18:08.205
-So we're cruising to North Philly.

00:18:08.272 --> 00:18:11.483
It's got the bad reputation, right?
Or depends where you're at?

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:15.044
-Depends where you're at
because so many people outside the city

00:18:15.788 --> 00:18:16.672
that's coming…

00:18:16.739 --> 00:18:20.221
Like New York, outside the city's
coming to move here.

00:18:20.665 --> 00:18:23.392
-There's a new building site there now.
-Oh, yeah.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:28.783
Growing up inner city, to get to a point
on some sense of happiness,

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:34.073
is far fetched because resources,
there's not a wide range

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.683
versus the suburb part.

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.274
Even a lot of schools that got closed down.

00:18:38.341 --> 00:18:40.623
A lot of public schools have closed down.

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:43.667
-Okay, I was asking off camera,
but why are you so positive?

00:18:43.734 --> 00:18:46.508
-Because coming from a city like Philly,

00:18:46.575 --> 00:18:49.845
where it can seem like
crabs in a barrel mentality,

00:18:49.912 --> 00:18:52.903
you gotta have that positive
'cause that's what keeps you going.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.369
Something to look forward to.

00:18:54.436 --> 00:18:55.632
Accomplishing a goal.

00:18:55.699 --> 00:18:58.172
That's why I like positivity, it helps.

00:18:58.239 --> 00:19:01.586
Versus looking at the other side
like someone sleeping in the street

00:19:01.653 --> 00:19:03.359
or got a needle in they arm.

00:19:03.426 --> 00:19:07.421
So growing up in North Philly
when you having that positive spirit

00:19:07.488 --> 00:19:09.168
or positive mindset can help.

00:19:09.835 --> 00:19:12.607
-Malcom, you gonna go off the clock
and cruise

00:19:12.674 --> 00:19:15.088
-You wanna do that?
-Let's go. It's completed.

00:19:15.155 --> 00:19:16.835
Five star rating, let's go.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.842
-Fishtown is that way?
-Fishtown is that way.

00:19:21.909 --> 00:19:24.084
If you went down Richmond Street,

00:19:24.151 --> 00:19:26.469
and got on 95 and off at Girad.

00:19:27.857 --> 00:19:29.297
-Girard.
-Girard, okay.

00:19:29.364 --> 00:19:30.454
Girad?

00:19:30.521 --> 00:19:33.155
And take that right down

00:19:33.222 --> 00:19:35.468
-All in there.
-No, speak deep Philly for me.

00:19:35.535 --> 00:19:37.036
-Girad, right?
-Girad.

00:19:37.103 --> 00:19:38.177
Girad, all right.

00:19:38.244 --> 00:19:41.153
-Get a waadaw.
-Get a waadaw, get a cawfee, getoudahere.

00:19:41.827 --> 00:19:43.932
-That's Jersey I'm speaking.
-[laughter]

00:19:43.999 --> 00:19:44.921
Cawfee, okay.

00:19:44.988 --> 00:19:48.331
So Fishtown is thriving,
there's restaurants, it's going on.

00:19:48.398 --> 00:19:50.783
-All kinds of restaurants.
-All kinds of people.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.486
They're moving from New York
'cause it's expensive.

00:19:53.553 --> 00:19:54.626
-They're moving in?

00:19:54.686 --> 00:19:59.134
All right, I live in
a 980 square foot roho.

00:19:59.208 --> 00:20:00.366
Lived there 30 years.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:02.807
The house next door to me,

00:20:02.874 --> 00:20:03.927
same size.

00:20:03.994 --> 00:20:06.391
-Yeah.
-No parking, schools suck.

00:20:06.458 --> 00:20:10.450
If your kids don't play soccer you gotta do
everything outside the neighborhood.

00:20:11.118 --> 00:20:12.783
-385.
-Wow.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:16.231
-Okay, then I'm gonna go to Kensington.
What are your thoughts there?

00:20:16.298 --> 00:20:18.638
Kensington is so sad.

00:20:18.705 --> 00:20:22.616
We don't even recognize our streets
but they did flip my mom and dad's house.

00:20:22.683 --> 00:20:24.556
Looks nice inside but…

00:20:24.623 --> 00:20:27.286
I was there two years ago, still as bad?

00:20:27.353 --> 00:20:28.236
-Yeah.
-Yep.

00:20:28.303 --> 00:20:29.990
Really? They haven't changed it?

00:20:30.057 --> 00:20:32.443
When the new mayor came in

00:20:32.973 --> 00:20:37.077
probably for like two months,
"We're cleaning up Kensington Ave."

00:20:37.718 --> 00:20:39.924
-They did nothing.
-For one day.

00:20:39.991 --> 00:20:41.452
They're all zombies.

00:20:41.519 --> 00:20:42.874
-It's bad.
-It's sad.

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:43.978
-Very sad.
-Okay.

00:20:44.045 --> 00:20:46.627
Across the street at Melrose Drug store,

00:20:46.694 --> 00:20:48.210
and they were selling…

00:20:49.629 --> 00:20:51.896
Train right across the street. That's K&amp;A!

00:20:51.963 --> 00:20:54.185
-Trotting over drug addicts.
-Yeah.

00:20:54.252 --> 00:20:56.503
It's actually sad.

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:58.988
Have you been? Are you from here?

00:20:59.055 --> 00:21:00.637
Yeah, born and raised.

00:21:00.704 --> 00:21:02.913
-Where at?
-North 23rd and Leon.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:03.875
Okay.

00:21:03.942 --> 00:21:05.914
-Nadavis High School.
-Okay.

00:21:05.981 --> 00:21:09.306
-What do you think of his fashion line?
That's his fashion line.

00:21:09.373 --> 00:21:11.053
-I think it looks nice.
-Thank you.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.800
My grandson would wear that.

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:17.137
Kensington always had a bit
of a reputation in the 70s.

00:21:17.661 --> 00:21:18.798
And it wasn't bad.

00:21:19.836 --> 00:21:22.248
-So what happened?
Manufacturing jobs went away?

00:21:22.315 --> 00:21:24.471
-All the manufacturing jobs.
-Everything.

00:21:24.538 --> 00:21:27.949
And then people start
just selling their property.

00:21:28.526 --> 00:21:29.789
Everybody, you know…

00:21:30.239 --> 00:21:31.893
I was born and raised there.

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:33.880
-Malcom lives in the 'burbs now.

00:21:34.387 --> 00:21:36.067
I live Delaware County now.

00:21:36.746 --> 00:21:37.807
Do you like it?

00:21:37.874 --> 00:21:41.316
I used to really love Philly,
"I'll never leave" but it's getting bad.

00:21:41.383 --> 00:21:43.199
-But they're making us leave.
-Yeah.

00:21:43.266 --> 00:21:45.315
You feel like you're getting pushed out?

00:21:45.382 --> 00:21:49.877
-I got pushed out of three neighborhoods.
-My property tax used to be $600.

00:21:49.944 --> 00:21:53.019
When I went up to $1,000
I said we can't complain

00:21:53.086 --> 00:21:55.336
we paid $600 all these years.

00:21:56.566 --> 00:21:58.430
Now they're $4,000.

00:21:58.497 --> 00:21:59.798
-Are you serious?

00:21:59.865 --> 00:22:01.399
They give you nothing.

00:22:01.466 --> 00:22:03.996
She's Fishtown,
I'm Port Richmond, I'm $2,800.

00:22:04.647 --> 00:22:06.724
-You're 28 years old?
-No… Oh, yeah…

00:22:06.791 --> 00:22:08.471
-[laughter]
-I had a hard life.

00:22:10.625 --> 00:22:12.080
You're looking great.

00:22:12.147 --> 00:22:16.190
-But you see people.
-My taxes are lower than hers.

00:22:18.525 --> 00:22:21.765
There's nurses down there
that used to be professionals.

00:22:21.832 --> 00:22:22.715
-Right.

00:22:23.389 --> 00:22:24.969
-It's sad.
-And Kenny…

00:22:25.036 --> 00:22:27.141
Malcom, you want to get out of the rain?

00:22:27.208 --> 00:22:28.766
Actually there's no cover here.

00:22:28.833 --> 00:22:31.081
-We good.
-We good. We good.

00:22:31.148 --> 00:22:32.361
You're hair's…

00:22:32.428 --> 00:22:33.916
When Kenny was the mayor…

00:22:33.983 --> 00:22:37.294
Listen, when Kenny did K&amp;A
cleaned it up 'cause someone was coming.

00:22:37.361 --> 00:22:38.244
-Yeah.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:40.907
They start walking around
our neighborhoods.

00:22:40.974 --> 00:22:43.805
Trying to get my water on
in front of my house.

00:22:43.872 --> 00:22:44.755
-Okay.

00:22:44.822 --> 00:22:47.802
Somebody came, I don't remember who it was.

00:22:48.353 --> 00:22:50.297
That was done, they were all right back

00:22:50.364 --> 00:22:52.608
-So what about World Cup?
You excited or no?

00:22:52.675 --> 00:22:53.749
I ain't watching.

00:22:54.493 --> 00:22:57.208
I mean this is like another world
from downtown, right?

00:22:57.275 --> 00:22:58.497
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:22:58.564 --> 00:23:00.833
-When you go down where I'm at…
-Yeah.

00:23:01.285 --> 00:23:03.327
-And you go like in…
-Very preppy.

00:23:03.394 --> 00:23:07.109
Down on Frankford Ave.
there's all kinds of world games.

00:23:07.176 --> 00:23:08.400
-Okay.

00:23:08.467 --> 00:23:11.093
 There's all kinds of festivities.

00:23:11.571 --> 00:23:12.479
Bye.

00:23:12.546 --> 00:23:13.683
Take care, ladies.

00:23:15.081 --> 00:23:16.937
-What do you got here?
-Soft pretzels.

00:23:17.004 --> 00:23:17.912
Yeah, sure.

00:23:17.979 --> 00:23:19.659
Thank you. Philly pretzels.

00:23:20.337 --> 00:23:22.006
That's Philly staple.

00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:23.427
Thank you.

00:23:23.494 --> 00:23:25.283
You'll never get a better pretzel.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.003
A summer dinner. Have fun.

00:23:28.478 --> 00:23:30.021
See ya, ladies. Thank you.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.343
-First Philly pretzel?
-Yeah.

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.622
These the menace.

00:23:33.689 --> 00:23:35.038
These pretzels win.

00:23:35.105 --> 00:23:36.368
You got the big one.

00:23:38.866 --> 00:23:41.473
If you can get 'em
when they first warm even better.

00:23:42.559 --> 00:23:43.443
-Nice, Malcom.

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:47.208
Did you think when you clocked in today

00:23:47.275 --> 00:23:50.279
you'd be walking around in the rain
eating Philly pretzels?

00:23:50.346 --> 00:23:52.279
-Talking to the ladies?
-You know…

00:23:52.346 --> 00:23:55.862
It's always an adventure with Uber.
You never know what's gonna happen.

00:23:55.929 --> 00:23:57.261
I look at it as like

00:23:57.328 --> 00:24:00.044
doing Uber's already
an adventure in itself.

00:24:00.506 --> 00:24:04.313
So why not further the adventure
with someone else that's adventurous?

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:06.073
You just gotta go with it

00:24:06.698 --> 00:24:08.277
We're getting rained out.

00:24:18.820 --> 00:24:20.772
[Peter] Malcom had to take a call.

00:24:20.839 --> 00:24:23.325
But these neighborhoods just go on forever.

00:24:24.343 --> 00:24:26.027
That used to be a German church.

00:24:26.530 --> 00:24:28.163
This is a Polish, Irish neighborhood.

00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:31.563
-Block party, is that what's going on?
-Yeah, it's a block party for…

00:24:32.678 --> 00:24:34.625
It's the baby's birthday, she's four.

00:24:35.087 --> 00:24:36.223
-Oh, that's cool.

00:24:36.290 --> 00:24:37.238
-Right, Harley?

00:24:37.305 --> 00:24:39.829
-You okay with her on camera?
-I don't know.

00:24:41.068 --> 00:24:42.883
Dad, is she okay to be on camera?

00:24:42.950 --> 00:24:44.951
-He's on a YouTube thing.
-Go ahead.

00:24:45.018 --> 00:24:45.933
You sure?

00:24:46.033 --> 00:24:49.399
He's a YouTube channel dude.
I've seen him a million times.

00:24:49.466 --> 00:24:51.667
-Tag my company in it.
-What's your company?

00:24:51.734 --> 00:24:54.633
-One Step Contracting.
-You're doing building, concrete?

00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:55.930
-How's it going?
-Good.

00:24:55.997 --> 00:24:59.600
I've seen him go to different states
and he's been in Philly for a minute

00:24:59.667 --> 00:25:03.325
and he does a lot of stuff in Philly,
what's going on here and there.

00:25:03.791 --> 00:25:07.617
Not like the news people
know the realities ofthe neighborhoods

00:25:07.684 --> 00:25:09.944
-What do the news people get wrong here?

00:25:10.011 --> 00:25:12.373
They don't know
their boundaries of the city. You

00:25:12.440 --> 00:25:16.237
gotta be in here to know
where the boundaries are for the city.

00:25:16.304 --> 00:25:20.077
-Is it okay if I stay under here?
-Yeah. Get in there.

00:25:20.144 --> 00:25:22.471
Don't call this Kensington on the news.

00:25:22.538 --> 00:25:24.357
-Don't call this Kensington?
-Yes!

00:25:24.424 --> 00:25:25.306
No. No.

00:25:25.373 --> 00:25:28.031
Don't call this Kensington
and don't call the other side Aramingo,

00:25:28.098 --> 00:25:31.033
Port Richmond, it's not. That's Jasper!

00:25:31.100 --> 00:25:32.964
-What is this?
-Port Richmond!

00:25:33.031 --> 00:25:35.432
Port Richmond!

00:25:35.499 --> 00:25:37.762
-This is part of the River Ward, Pennsport,

00:25:38.274 --> 00:25:40.357
Port Richmond, Bridesburg.

00:25:40.424 --> 00:25:42.008
We're all the River Ward.

00:25:42.075 --> 00:25:44.915
Are you guys getting fired up
for the birthday?

00:25:44.982 --> 00:25:48.133
I keep flags all day every day.

00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:49.522
Irish ones and…

00:25:49.930 --> 00:25:51.192
Back to back.

00:25:51.259 --> 00:25:53.033
-That's your place?
-Yes.

00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:55.983
-You're doing a great job.
-Philly is where it all started.

00:25:56.050 --> 00:25:58.793
-Of course we're about the 250.
-The origin story.

00:25:58.860 --> 00:26:02.350
Philly's many things, huh?
